1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:07,000
I am Nikhil Singh Bisht, presenting OmniDirector AI for the Meta Global AI Developer Hackathon.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:14,000
In live broadcasting, esports, and podcasting, a multi-camera production requires an entire human crew:

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:22,500
A technical director switching cameras, and an editor spending 10 hours cutting widescreen video into vertical reels.

4
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:28,500
OmniDirector AI eliminates this bottleneck by acting as an autonomous virtual control room...

5
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:33,730
...running directly in your browser, powered by Meta's frontier generative models.

6
00:00:33,730 --> 00:00:44,700
Here in our studio, we are connected to Baseten's serverless infrastructure, running Meta's open-weights Muse Spark Open with 2M TPM rate limit.

7
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:51,200
With our multi-cloud switcher, we can dynamically route between Baseten and the official Meta Model API Cloud with zero downtime...

8
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:57,620
...ensuring continuous 24/7 broadcast reliability across all camera channels.

9
00:00:57,620 --> 00:01:06,100
Unlike crude volume-based switchers, Meta Muse Spark arbitrates cuts based on conversational pacing, speaker dominance, and narrative climax beats.

10
00:01:06,100 --> 00:01:16,600
It enforces professional pacing rules—holding shots for a minimum of 2.5 seconds to prevent frantic switching.

11
00:01:16,600 --> 00:01:23,500
And notice our hardware resilience sentinel: if a camera feed disconnects or goes offline...

12
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:31,390
...the director instantly detects the status and holds the broadcast safely on live cameras, guaranteeing zero black frames.

13
00:01:31,390 --> 00:01:36,400
Next is Meta SAM 3.1 zero-shot segmentation.

14
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:44,900
At any moment during a live broadcast, a creator can click directly on any subject or object on the 4K canvas.

15
00:01:44,900 --> 00:01:52,900
In under 15 milliseconds, SAM 3.1 extracts sub-pixel polygonal boundary contours and confidence tags...

16
00:01:52,900 --> 00:01:57,590
...enabling dynamic focal tracking and green-screen-free subject isolation in real time.

17
00:01:57,590 --> 00:02:05,600
Now for the biggest game-changer for creators: automated 9:16 vertical reel synthesis while the 16:9 widescreen broadcast runs.

18
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:13,600
OmniDirector uses computer vision and physical spring damping to smoothly glide the vertical viewport across subjects.

19
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:18,600
It keeps the active speaker perfectly center-staged with zero jerky movements, accompanied by synchronized karaoke captions.

20
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:23,170
With one click on 'Export Reel', it records a broadcast-ready vertical highlight clip ready for immediate social publishing.

21
00:02:23,170 --> 00:02:31,700
For traditional video editors, OmniDirector exports a standard CMX 3600 Edit Decision List.

22
00:02:31,700 --> 00:02:38,700
You can drop this straight into DaVinci Resolve or Premiere Pro to instantly recreate every AI cut on your multi-cam timeline.

23
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:45,700
And with our Meta Payloads drawer, developers can inspect the exact system prompts, JSON contracts, and multimodal schemas.

24
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:52,420
We've also built in both a clean Scandinavian Light theme and a sleek Dark studio mode.

25
00:02:52,420 --> 00:02:58,900
OmniDirector AI brings broadcast television automation directly to solo creators and indie studios worldwide...

26
00:02:58,900 --> 00:03:04,400
...showcasing the true power of Meta's multimodal AI ecosystem.

27
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:08,230
Thank you for watching, and happy building!
